The song within a song;
The Wreck of the Edmund Fitzgerald
is a 1976 song in tribute to the sinking of the bulk carrier SS Edmund Fitzgerald on Lake Superior. Lightfoot was inspired to write the ballad after he read an article on the disaster in Newsweek magazine. It reached number 1 in Canada and was his second song ever to hit the top ten, including staying in the top ten for a week in the U.S. Lightfoot was especially proud of it because it made such a depressing subject into a commercial success.
